# Build artifacts
build/
build-*/
bin/
tmp/
dist/
*.o
*.a
*.so

# Generated recompiler output (derived from copyrighted ROM, never committed)
src/gen/

# ROMs and dumps (Legal requirement: no proprietary game assets in repo)
*.sfc
*.smc
*.bin
*.sav
*.srm

# AES internal - local project management, never committed.
#
# BUT: the peer-review protocol requires a pre-registered rubric committed with
# its hash, and an un-reviewable protocol is worse than a slightly untidy tree.
# The aes-peer-review skill ships only SKILL.md - the protocol spec and rubric
# templates live in the sibling `aes` skill - so the rubric for this project is
# authored here and must be committable.
#
# `aes/*` rather than `aes/` because git cannot re-include a subdirectory whose
# parent is excluded. Everything under aes/ stays ignored except the rubric and
# the review record.
aes/*
!aes/templates/
!aes/peer-reviews/
.aes/

# snesrecomp specific
rom.cfg
mods/preloaded/packages/*.snesmod
.snesrecomp-cache.json

# IDE and tooling
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store

# Test outputs
Testing/
*.log

# Docker
.docker/saves/
last_run_report.json
states/

# Peer study frontend artefacts. The frontend now anchors these to the
# executable's own directory, but a relative path once wrote a 128 KiB WRAM dump
# into the repository root, so ignore them defensively.
jjwram.*.bin
jj.srm
jj.srm.bak
